📘 TOPIC SHEET 2: Tool Selection
(Business Rule vs Flow vs Workflow vs Plugin vs Custom API)
~15 questions in exam — #1 MOST TESTED TOPIC ⚠️
________________________________________
📖 Concept
The exam constantly asks: "Which tool should you use?"
Tool	Runs Where	Code?	Cross-Table?	Returns Value?	Real-Time?
Business Rule	Client-side (form) or Table-level	❌ No code	❌ Same table only	❌ No	✅ Yes (instant on form)
Power Automate Cloud Flow	Cloud (server)	❌ No code	✅ Yes	❌ No (unless child flow)	⚠️ Near real-time (seconds delay)
Classic Workflow	Server (async or real-time)	❌ No code	⚠️ Limited	❌ No	✅ If set to real-time
Plugin	Server (sync/async)	✅ C# code	✅ Yes	✅ Yes	✅ Yes
Custom API	Server	✅ Code	✅ Yes	✅ Yes	✅ Yes
Desktop Flow	Local machine	❌ No code (recorded)	N/A	⚠️ Via output params	❌ Scheduled/triggered
🧠 Decision Tree (MEMORIZE THIS)
Need to SET/VALIDATE/SHOW/HIDE field on a FORM?
  → Business Rule

Need to SEND EMAIL when record changes?
  → Power Automate Cloud Flow (or Classic Workflow if real-time needed)

Need to automate a LEGACY APP with no API?
  → Desktop Flow

Need logic across MULTIPLE TABLES + RETURN A VALUE?
  → Custom API

Need server-side logic WITH CODE?
  → Plugin

Need to UPDATE STATUS in REAL-TIME (no delay)?
  → Classic Workflow (real-time) with Change Status step

"No custom code allowed" in scenario?
  → ELIMINATE Plugin and Custom API immediately
________________________________________
🔑 Rules to Memorize
Rule	Remember
1	Business Rule = form-level logic ONLY (set value, show/hide, validate, set required, recommend)
2	Canvas apps business rules: can ONLY validate, set values, set required — CANNOT show/hide or recommend
3	"No custom code" in the question = eliminate Plugin + Custom API
4	Real-time update = Classic Workflow with Change Status step (NOT cloud flow — cloud flows have delay)
5	Cross-table logic + return value = Custom API
6	Legacy app, no API = Desktop Flow
7	Send email on trigger = Power Automate Cloud Flow
8	Approval process = Power Automate Cloud Flow (Approvals connector)
9	Daily/weekly scheduled task = Scheduled Cloud Flow
10	Wunderlist/3rd-party integration = Power Automate (connector-based)
________________________________________
📝 All Related Questions + Answers
Q8: Three automation requirements
•	Send email when status changes on Opportunity → Classic Workflow (real-time email on status change)
•	Text sales manager when Opportunity created → Power Automate (SMS connector)
•	Create Wunderlist task when open 30 days → Power Automate (scheduled check + Wunderlist connector)
________________________________________
Q17: Dynamic field visibility in canvas app
Scenario: Vet office, dropdown "type of pet" → if "Other" selected, show text field
Answer: ✅ Business Rule — show/hide based on field value
⚠️ BUT: Canvas apps DON'T support show/hide in business rules. This question likely expects conditional visibility using Power Fx (If formula on Visible property)
Exam tip: If the question says "canvas app" + "show/hide" → it might be a Power Fx formula, not business rule
________________________________________
Q40-41: Three business logic scenarios
•	Set field value automatically when record is saved → Business Rule
•	Automatically send email when record is created → Power Automate
•	Validate data before save → Business Rule
________________________________________
Q140: Three automation processes
•	Automate legacy software with no API → Desktop Flow
•	Access data from REST API → Custom Connector (in Power Automate)
•	Access public web data with OAuth → Custom Connector
________________________________________
Q160: Complex logic, return value, run from existing action
Answer: ✅ Custom API
Why not Plugin? Custom API can be called from existing Dataverse actions and returns values. Plugin runs on events but isn't callable as an action
Why not Workflow? Workflows can't return values
Why not Flow? Flows don't return values to Dataverse natively
________________________________________
Q163: Two requirements
•	Prevent save if custom validation fails → Real-time Workflow (runs before save, can cancel)
•	Query and update a list of records → Cloud Flow (List Rows + Update Row actions)
________________________________________
Q167: Two email requirements
•	Send email in real-time when customer enters email → Real-time Workflow
•	Send email at same time every day for cases open > 24hrs → Scheduled Cloud Flow
________________________________________
Q212: Create evaluation record automatically for a prospect
Answer: ✅ Cloud Flow (triggered when prospect record created → auto-create evaluation)
Why not Quick Create Form? Evaluation records "cannot be manually created" per requirements
Why not Plugin? "Custom code not allowed" per case study
________________________________________
Q215-218, Q223: Auto-update Status in real-time (Yes/No Series)
•	Flow with Update Item action → ❌ No (Update Item is SharePoint, not Dataverse)
•	Workflow with Update Record step → ❌ No (Update Record doesn't change status)
•	Flow with Update a Row action → ❌ No (cloud flows have delay, not truly real-time)
•	Workflow with Change Status step → ✅ Yes (real-time workflow + Change Status = instant)
🔥 Key Lesson: For real-time status changes, use Classic Workflow with Change Status step. Cloud Flows are near-real-time but have inherent delay.
________________________________________
Q169-170: Approval process without code
Answer: ✅ Power Automate Cloud Flow (Approvals connector)
Why not PCF? PCF is a UI component, not process automation
Why not Azure Service Bus? Overkill and requires code/configuration
________________________________________
Q164: Canvas app — button to send email
Answer: ✅ Power Automate Cloud Flow (triggered from canvas app button)
Why not Classic Workflow? Can't trigger from canvas app button
Why not BPF? BPF is for guided processes, not single actions
________________________________________
